==============================================================================
  Mutation tests  (assertion-strength validation)
==============================================================================

  Strategy: replace each named fact's body with `{}` (no constraint),
  then re-run Alloy. Each listed assertion should now FAIL on the
  mutated model. If it still PASSes, the assertion is vacuous and
  must be strengthened.

  - MUTATE F_CareTeamGating  → runs/C-L2/mutated_F_CareTeamGating.als
    rationale: Removing F_CareTeamGating allows Alloy to construct a world where a clinical user without any active care-team row has Permitted outcome on RecordsLookup or AddNote. The injection forces exactly that scenario, which OwnershipBasedAccess and FR_004_CareTeamGating are designed to catch.
    expected to FAIL: OwnershipBasedAccess, FR_004_CareTeamGating
      - OwnershipBasedAccess: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_004_CareTeamGating: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_NoteLinkedToOperation  → runs/C-L2/mutated_F_NoteLinkedToOperation.als
    rationale: Removing F_NoteLinkedToOperation allows a ClinicalNote to exist that is not produced by any Operation, or to be claimed by two different Operations, violating the append-only and one-creator invariants. The injection forces two distinct operations to reference the same note, which AppendOnly and FR_011_NotesAppendOnly catch.
    expected to FAIL: AppendOnly, FR_011_NotesAppendOnly
      - AppendOnly: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_011_NotesAppendOnly: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_AuditEntriesAppendOnly  → runs/C-L2/mutated_F_AuditEntriesAppendOnly.als
    rationale: Removing F_AuditEntriesAppendOnly allows two distinct Operations to share a single AuditEntry, violating both the one-audit-per-operation invariant and the immutability/append-only guarantee. The injection forces exactly that.
    expected to FAIL: AppendOnly, AuditCompleteness, FR_012_AlwaysOnAudit, FR_014_AuditImmutable
      - AppendOnly: PASS (vacuous?)
      - AuditCompleteness: PASS (vacuous?)
      - FR_012_AlwaysOnAudit: PASS (vacuous?)
      - FR_014_AuditImmutable: PASS (vacuous?)

  - MUTATE F_LeastPrivilegeEnforced  → runs/C-L2/mutated_F_LeastPrivilegeEnforced.als
    rationale: Removing F_LeastPrivilegeEnforced allows a HospitalAdministrator to have a Permitted RecordsLookup or AddNote outcome, which LeastPrivilege is designed to catch. The injection forces that forbidden cell to be present.
    expected to FAIL: LeastPrivilege, FR_005_AdminCannotAccessClinicalContent, FR_017_AdminOnlyAuditSearch
      - LeastPrivilege: PASS (vacuous?)
      - FR_005_AdminCannotAccessClinicalContent: PASS (vacuous?)
      - FR_017_AdminOnlyAuditSearch: PASS (vacuous?)

  - MUTATE F_NoteAuthorIsClinical  → runs/C-L2/mutated_F_NoteAuthorIsClinical.als
    rationale: Removing F_NoteAuthorIsClinical allows a ClinicalNote to have noteAuthorRole = HospitalAdministrator, which the data-model CHECK and FR-005 prohibit. The injection forces a note whose author role is the administrator role.
    expected to FAIL: FR_010_NoteAuthorIsClinical, FR_005_AdminCannotAccessClinicalContent
      - FR_010_NoteAuthorIsClinical: PASS (vacuous?)
      - FR_005_AdminCannotAccessClinicalContent: PASS (vacuous?)

  - MUTATE F_AuditNoteIdConstraint  → runs/C-L2/mutated_F_AuditNoteIdConstraint.als
    rationale: Removing F_AuditNoteIdConstraint allows an AuditEntry with aeOutcome=Denied to carry a non-null aeNoteRef, which would leak the existence of a note to a denied accessor and violate the structural CHECK in the data model. The injection forces a denied audit entry to carry a note reference.
    expected to FAIL: FR_013_AuditNoteIdConstraint, NoInformationLeakage
      - FR_013_AuditNoteIdConstraint: FAIL (expected)
      - NoInformationLeakage: FAIL (expected)

